    "narrative": "The run did not find broad deterioration in net margin at these companies. Instead, it found that revenue growth explained the observed margin change, so the margin movement looked more like a growth effect than a clean decline in margin quality.\n\nThe claim that net margin had deteriorated over the recent periods was rejected: there was some evidence for it, but more evidence pointed against it. The claim that revenue growth was the explanation was supported strongly, with no refuting evidence recorded.\n\nThe analysis ran repeated trend-break checks, time-series trend analyses, change-point detection, and a distribution summary, and it stopped because the evidence was sufficient. Two questions remained open: whether the margin change was sustained across the recent periods or just a one-off fluctuation, and whether the timing of revenue growth aligned with the margin movement or diverged.",
    "statement": "Supported: Revenue growth is the explanation for the observed margin change. | Not supported: Net margin has deteriorated over the recent periods for these companies.",
